<!-- ABOUT PAGE -->
<section class="about-section">
  <div class="about-inner">
    <h2>About Forma</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Forma — Student Intelligence Platform</strong> is a premium
      student management interface built for the Cognifyz IT Solutions Full
      Stack Development Internship. This is the Task 2 deliverable.
    </p>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-card">
        <h3>What it does</h3>
        <p>
          Register students with full academic details, validate every piece of
          information on both the browser and the server, and browse searchable
          student records. Every submitted record receives a registration
          reference.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-card">
        <h3>Task 2 features</h3>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li>Extended registration form (9 fields including Terms and Conditions)</li>
          <li>Real-time inline JavaScript validation</li>
          <li>Express server-side validation (independent of the browser)</li>
          <li>Preserved form values after validation errors</li>
          <li>In-memory temporary storage</li>
          <li>Student records with search and course filtering</li>
          <li>Responsive dark SaaS-style interface</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="about-card">
        <h3>Technology stack</h3>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li>Node.js</li>
          <li>Express.js</li>
          <li>EJS server-side rendering</li>
          <li>HTML5, CSS3, Vanilla JavaScript</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="about-card">
        <h3>Storage &amp; security</h3>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li>In-memory array (resets on server restart)</li>
          <li>No MongoDB or external database</li>
          <li>All output HTML-escaped in EJS templates</li>
          <li>Allowlist validation for course, gender, and other fields</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="about-note">
      <p><strong>Important:</strong> Student records are stored temporarily in
      server memory only. Restarting the server clears all records. This is by
      design for Task 2; a future task may integrate a persistent database.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="about-actions">
      <a href="/" class="btn btn-outline">Register a Student</a>
      <a href="/students" class="btn btn-primary">View Student Records</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
